    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "24d1831a5915eab091827a1651c241f44206b1086014fb4352ec33cf862d2e5a",
      "text": "In the morning, you’ll travel to Puno by private vehicle. The journey takes about **10 hours**, with lunch and sightseeing stops included.\n\nYour first stop is the **Church of San Pedro de Andahuaylillas**, built in the 16th century on a site that was sacred to the Incas. Its richly decorated interior earned it the name ‘Sistine Chapel of the Andes’. Inside, you’ll find murals by Luis de Riaño, a ceiling decorated with gold leaf and a carved Baroque altar.\n\nNext, you’ll visit the Inca temple at Raqchi, the high-altitude La Raya Pass and the museum in Pukara. Lunch is at a simple local restaurant.\n\nYou’ll stay in a **Superior Room** at the **GHL Hotel Lago Titicaca**.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-e805e5042bc7",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      }
